{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The heat shrink tubing and solder seal connectors felt relevant because they help insulate and protect wiring connections, a clear continuation of my earlier wire terminal purchase.",
    "The epoxy fits my interest in practical repair adhesives, as suggested by my tape and vinyl cement purchases, although I would wait for a specific repair before buying that much."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Cutting wheels, feeler gauges and electronic cleaner address tasks I have not shown a need for; buying repair supplies does not mean I currently need to cut metal, measure gaps or clean electronics.",
    "The nuts and tap kit require an exact thread-size match, while the large super glue refill assumes woodworking needs I have not expressed. The magnets also lack a clear connection to a current task."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My purchases seem to have been treated as a broad interest in workshop supplies, even though I choose items for particular practical uses.",
    "My adhesive purchases seem to imply interest in any adhesive, overlooking differences in material, purpose and quantity."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "A useful connection is how an item complements supplies I already bought, such as insulation for electrical terminals, rather than simply belonging in a workshop.",
    "I need a concrete use before choosing specialized tools or exact-size parts, and even a relevant repair product can be too large a commitment without a specific job."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my practical repair interests but stretched them into specialized tasks and quantities that my history does not justify."
}"}
